BetterString.mcp/BetterString.mcp

    NAME
        BetterString.mcp -- Edit BetterString preferences.

    SUPERCLASS
        Mccprefs.mui

    DESCRIPTION
        Provide preference controls for BetterString.mcc. This source defines
        version 11.33 and requires muimaster version 19. BetterString.mcc is
        listed as a used class. The header declares the class and
        configuration-item IDs, but no own MUI attributes or methods.
        The nine settings comprise two backgrounds, five pens and two
        selection options. Configuration IDs are dataspace keys, not SetAttrs
        tags. The inherited Settingsgroup methods exchange their values; this
        class does not itself write a preferences file.
        AROS defaults: ActiveBack "2:m1", ActiveText "m5", InactiveBack
        "2:m2", InactiveText "m4", Cursor "m0", MarkedBack "m5", MarkedText
        "m0", SelectOnActive FALSE, SelectPointer TRUE. Each name has the
        MUICFG_BetterString_ prefix. Font and Frame are obsolete IDs removed
        on export.

    NOTES
        The code treats muimaster 20.5500 or later as MUI4 and disables both
        background controls. It disables SelectPointer when the example
        reports a non-normal PointerType. Disabled controls still participate
        in configuration exchange. These are version and attribute checks, not
        an AROS capability guarantee.
        The group installs no notifications to apply edited preferences to the
        example field. Shortcut labels are help text; consult BetterString.mcc
        for implemented editing behavior.
        On AROS the icon uses NBitmap when its probed version is at least 15.8
        and creation succeeds, otherwise Bodychunk. Missing catalog text uses
        built-in strings. The standalone Preference.c uses a Group-derived
        class and invokes no configuration transfer or preferences saving.
BetterString.mcp/OM_NEW

    NAME
        BetterString.mcp/OM_NEW -- Create the preferences group.

    SYNOPSIS
        obj = NewObject(class, NULL, TAG_DONE);

    FUNCTION
        Call the superclass constructor, create the controls and attach their
        group. At muimaster 20.0 or later, register all nine controls with
        Mccprefs_RegisterGadget. No initial dataspace is loaded.

    INPUTS
        class -- A valid BetterString.mcp class. Supply inherited construction
        tags as required by Mccprefs.

    RESULT
        The new object, or NULL if superclass or group construction fails.
        Group failure disposes the superclass object. AddMember and
        RegisterGadget results are not checked.

    NOTES
        Dispose through MUI after use. Keep catalog-backed text available
        while controls use it. This implements an inherited method; it is not
        a new method identifier.
BetterString.mcp/MUIM_Settingsgroup_ConfigToGadgets

    NAME
        MUIM_Settingsgroup_ConfigToGadgets -- Load preference controls.

    SYNOPSIS
        DoMethod(obj, MUIM_Settingsgroup_ConfigToGadgets, configdata);

    FUNCTION
        Find each of nine items with Dataspace_Find, using its default when
        absent. Assign string specifications to image/pen attributes and
        dereference integer data as IPTR for the two checkmarks. Suppress
        attribute notifications.

    INPUTS
        obj -- An initialized BetterString.mcp object.
        configdata -- A live dataspace. Present strings must be valid
        NUL-terminated specifications. Present integers must contain a
        readable, appropriately aligned IPTR in the native representation.

    RESULT
        Always zero. This is not a load-success report.

    NOTES
        No size, type or schema validation is performed. Keep input storage
        valid throughout the synchronous calls; subsequent string ownership
        follows the receiving gadgets. The method does not copy the dataspace
        or write a file. Use the UI in its owning application context.
BetterString.mcp/MUIM_Settingsgroup_GadgetsToConfig

    NAME
        MUIM_Settingsgroup_GadgetsToConfig -- Export preference controls.

    SYNOPSIS
        DoMethod(obj, MUIM_Settingsgroup_GadgetsToConfig, configdata);

    FUNCTION
        Read all nine controls. Compare strings to defaults without case
        sensitivity. Add a nondefault string including its NUL, or remove a
        matching-default key. Add a nondefault integer using sizeof(SIPTR), or
        remove its default-valued key. Finally remove obsolete Font and Frame
        keys.

    INPUTS
        obj -- An initialized BetterString.mcp object with readable
        specification strings.
        configdata -- A live mutable dataspace. It is modified synchronously;
        unrelated keys are retained.

    RESULT
        Always zero. Add and Remove results are ignored; a complete or atomic
        update is not guaranteed.

    NOTES
        Disabled controls are included. Matching-default entries are removed
        rather than preserving explicit defaults or capitalization. Integer
        data follows the build ABI without endian or word-size conversion.
        Dataspace_Add receives string pointers or a temporary integer address
        and must copy bytes during the call. File saving belongs to the caller
        or preference framework.

